; mini-prolog (docs/plans/plan_prolog.md): Edinburgh's Prolog, the
; standard's core, written here: Prolog (the terms, the operators, a
; term written), Prolog_read (a text's clauses, by the operators'
; priorities), Prolog_db (a predicate's clauses as they are kept),
; Prolog_machine (unification and its trail, the goals to prove and the
; choice points as data, the cut, catch and throw, the tracer's four
; ports), Prolog_prelude (append, member, bagof, the grammars' rules...
; in Prolog), Prolog_builtins (is, the atoms', assert, write, consult).
; And the second machine, -wam: Wam (Warren's instructions), Wam_compile
; (a clause compiled to them, the index on the first argument, the
; listing), Wam_machine (the registers, the environments, the choice
; points; put in Prolog_machine as its engine).
(library
 (name ix_prolog)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules :standard \ CLI Main)
 (libraries ix_core))

; the command
(library
 (name ix_prolog_cli)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules CLI)
 (libraries ix_prolog ix_core fpath caps))

(executable
 (name Main)
 (public_name mini-prolog)
 (package ix)
 (modules Main)
 (libraries ix_prolog_cli ix_core caps))
